    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0458" n="426" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v19/pg426"/>

                <head>258. Memorandum From the President’s Special Assistant (Rostow) to President Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d258-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1967-06-10T17:05:00-04:00">June 10, 1967, 5:05 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. President:</p>
                <p>These intercepts<anchor n="2" xml:id="d258-f2"/>—showing some honest ambiguity
                    about the ship after the attack—suggest that there may have been a breakdown of
                    communications on the Israeli side; that is, the tactical base which first
                    received word that the ship was American may not have flashed that information
                    to other air force and naval units.</p>
                <p>We shall, of course, analyze this affair further.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        Walt
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
